[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:What's for Supper?]
[00:01.20]What kind of fish are they? | 它们是什么鱼？
[00:13.60]Fish and chips has always been a favourite dish in Britain, | 炸鱼薯条一直是英国人最喜欢的菜肴，
[00:19.44]but as the oceans have been overfished, fish has become more and more expensive. | 但由于海洋被过度捕捞，鱼类变得越来越昂贵。
[00:26.74]So it comes as a surprise to learn that giant fish are terrifying the divers on North Sea oil rigs. | 因此，当得知巨型鱼类正在恐吓北海石油钻井平台的潜水员时，这令人感到惊讶。
[00:36.64]Oil rigs have to be repaired frequently and divers, who often have to work in darkness a hundred feet under water, | 石油钻井平台需要经常维修，而潜水员通常必须在水下百英尺的黑暗中工作，
[00:46.91]have been frightened out of their wits by giant fish bumping into them as they work. | 他们在工作时被撞到他们的巨型鱼吓得魂不附体。
[00:54.32]Now they have had special cages made to protect them from these monsters. | 现在他们已经制造了特殊的笼子来保护他们免受这些“怪物”的侵害。
[01:00.62]The fish are not sharks or killer whales, | 这些鱼不是鲨鱼也不是虎鲸，
[01:04.72]but favourite eating varieties like cod and skate which grow to unnatural sizes, | 而是人们喜欢吃的品种，比如鳕鱼和鳐鱼，它们长得异常大，
[01:12.67]sometimes as much as twelve feet in length. | 有时甚至长达十二英尺。
[01:17.16]Three factors have caused these fish to grow so large: | 有三个因素导致这些鱼长得如此巨大：
[01:22.62]the warm water round the hot oil pipes under the sea; | 海底热油管道周围的温暖水域；
[01:27.68]the plentiful supply of food thrown overboard by the crews on the rigs; | 钻井平台船员扔到海里的丰富食物供应；
[01:34.20]the total absence of fishing boats around the oil rigs. | 以及石油钻井平台周围完全没有渔船。
[01:39.29]As a result, the fish just eat and eat and grow and grow in the lovely warm water. | 结果，这些鱼就在这宜人的暖水中不停地吃，不停地长大。
[01:48.70]Who eats who? | 到底是谁吃了谁？